WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.420
A person has had their thyroid removed.

2
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:08.420
They take only thyroxine, called T4.

3
00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:12.480
Yet their blood still holds the more active hormone, T3.

4
00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:14.100
Where does it come from?

5
00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:17.240
If the gland were the only source, there should be none.

6
00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:20.310
The thyroid secretes mostly T4.

7
00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:24.850
T4 binds the thyroid hormone receptor much more weakly than T3 does.

8
00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:28.010
So T4 is best treated as a prohormone.

9
00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:32.510
Inside cells, T3 binds receptors that regulate transcription.

10
00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:34.670
That is the form that acts.

11
00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:38.870
Tissues contain three enzymes called deiodinases.

12
00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:40.750
Each removes one iodine.

13
00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:45.790
D1 and D2 remove an iodine from the outer ring of T4.

14
00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:49.250
That makes T3, and it switches the hormone on.

15
00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:52.710
D3 removes an iodine from the inner ring instead.

16
00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:57.650
That turns T4 into reverse T3, which is inactive.

17
00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:01.770
The ring that loses the iodine decides: on or off.

18
00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:06.140
In 1970, Braverman, Ingbar and Sterling tested this.

19
00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:09.300
They studied 13 patients treated with T4.

20
00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:15.080
All but two were athyreotic, meaning without a functioning thyroid, or hypothyroid.

21
00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:20.000
They gave labelled T4, and separated the iodine compounds of serum by

22
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.900
chromatography. Labelled T3 appeared.

23
00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:29.500
A specially purified lot of tracer held less than 0.1 % T3, and gave the same

24
00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:35.360
result. In two more patients, T4 went into a vein, bypassing the gut.

25
00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:37.500
Labelled T3 still appeared.

26
00:01:38.333 --> 00:01:42.393
The result ruled in conversion outside the thyroid, in humans.

27
00:01:43.073 --> 00:01:46.113
The study did not identify the enzyme or the organ.

28
00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:49.633
It did not measure how much T3 is made this way.

29
00:01:50.253 --> 00:01:55.453
Later work is commonly summarized as roughly 80 percent, in healthy people with

30
00:01:55.453 --> 00:01:58.193
enough iodine. That is an approximate estimate.

31
00:01:59.067 --> 00:02:01.407
Hormone does not simply diffuse into cells.

32
00:02:01.847 --> 00:02:04.707
It enters through transporters such as MCT8.

33
00:02:05.287 --> 00:02:09.247
Inside the cell, D2 often makes T3 from T4.

34
00:02:09.747 --> 00:02:14.267
So the T3 inside a cell need not match the T3 in plasma.

35
00:02:14.827 --> 00:02:20.267
In mice lacking D2, body temperature fell in the cold, because brown fat made less

36
00:02:20.267 --> 00:02:23.287
heat. Yet plasma T3 was normal.

37
00:02:23.967 --> 00:02:29.567
Keep the rule. The thyroid sends mostly T4, and the ring that loses its iodine

38
00:02:29.567 --> 00:02:31.427
decides: on or off.
